fheroes2 for RISC OS
====================

fheroes2 is a free, open source re-creation of the game engine of
Heroes of Might and Magic II. This is a port of fheroes2 to RISC OS 5
(tested on the Raspberry Pi 4). It runs in a desktop window or full
screen.

Version: see the Version file in the docs directory.


You need the original game's data
---------------------------------
fheroes2 is only the engine. You need the data from the original game
(GOG or CD) or from the free demo:

  https://archive.org/download/HeroesofMightandMagicIITheSuccessionWars_1020/h2demo.zip

From the game (or the demo zip), copy the DATA and MAPS directories
(and ANIM and MUSIC if you have them) into !fheroes2, next to !Run.
To open the application directory, hold Shift and double-click it.

Or put them anywhere you like and set fheroes2$Data to that directory,
for example in your !Boot:

  Set fheroes2$Data ADFS::HardDisc4.$.Games.HoMM2

The demo has one map (Broken Alliance); the full game has the
campaigns and all the maps.


Requirements
------------
- RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine (Raspberry Pi 2 or later recommended)
- For sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager, in ssb.zip from
    https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html
  (merge its !System with yours). SharedSound is part of RISC OS. John
  Duffell's own site (now on the Internet Archive) has more details:
    https://web.archive.org/web/20110920080106/http://www.duffell.riscos.me.uk/
  Without them the game plays silently.
- The ARMEABISupport module and SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later (both
  can be installed with !PackMan).
- PThreadTicker 0.03 (from UnixLib 5.0.3.2) is included; !Run loads it
  unless your !System already has it.


Playing
-------
- Double-click !fheroes2. The game opens a 640 x 480 window; choose a
  bigger resolution in the game's System options ("Resolution").
- Full screen: F4, or in the game's graphics settings. The game
  stays a desktop task in full screen.
- The game draws its own mouse pointer, so the desktop pointer is
  hidden while it is over the game window.
- Quit from the game's menu, the window's close icon, or the icon bar.


Where things are saved
----------------------
Settings, saved games and the log of high scores go in
<Choices$Write>.fheroes2.


Music
-----
The original game's music is MIDI. RISC OS has no MIDI synthesiser, so
the game plays it with its own one (riscos-midisynth, TinySoundFont)
and the SoundFont in files.soundfonts (TimGM6mb). You can put another
.sf2 file there instead. The GOG version's OGG music tracks aren't
supported yet.


Logging
-------
Test builds write a log to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.fheroes2log. If something
goes wrong, please send it along with what you did. To turn it off,
edit !Run (see the Logging section).


